e so  it really depends of course if  there are so many potential analyze of  course for an analyze which is  very important very often used like for  example ascorbic acid  you will find different quality levels  available  but for more let's say niche compounds  that are not so often tested usually  it's not economically  feasible to to do the certification to  crm  so then there's only an analytical  standards grade  available but also there might be other  examples like the  marine toxins where the material is very  expensive the starting material  so actually the cost difference isn't  even  so high between an analytical standard  and the crm grade  so there it wouldn't make sense to offer  an analytical standard and you only have  the crm  so you can see it really it really  depends  on on which compound it is  but we we cannot offer all the quality  grades for all  for all the products  dr noel thank you again for your time  today and for your important research  and before we go i want to thank the  audience for joining us today and for  their interesting questions  questions that we did not have time for  today and those submitted during the  on-demand period  will be addressed by our speaker via  contact information  you provide at the time of registration  and i also want to thank our sponsor  millapor sigma  for today's webinar this webcast can be  viewed on demand through june of 2021  until next time take care be safe  bye-bye now  you

